{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>On Mount Sinai, etc.</b> One needs to know why He mentioned Mount Sinai in connection with this commandment. And although our Sages of blessed memory said (Torat Kohanim) that it comes to teach that all the commandments were stated in their general principles and their specific details at Sinai, there is still room for our question: why did He teach this specifically in this commandment in particular, and not in the first commandment or the last one? Perhaps it is because, since He mentioned the gift of the land, as it is written <b>which I am giving</b>, He was precise to say 'on Mount Sinai,' to say that by virtue of Mount Sinai — meaning, what they received upon it — the gift was completed, for on condition of Torah HaShem gave the land." "<b>Further,</b> according to the statement of the Gemara, tractate Avodah Zarah (Avodah Zarah 20a), which the Rambam ruled in chapter 3 of the Laws of Acquisition, and this is its language: it is forbidden to give a gentile a free gift — end quote. And if so, Israel before they received the Torah have the status of gentiles, and after receiving the Torah He may give them. Therefore He said <b>on Mount Sinai</b>, for through this He can say, 'which I am giving to you.' And through this it is also resolved why it was necessary to say 'which I am giving,' for it is obvious that He is the One who gives and there is no other to dispute it. And you will find that in parashat Kedoshim (Leviticus 19:23) He said, 'When you come into the land and plant,' etc., and there He did not need to state a sign for it — except that He intended what we have written. From this point onward it is resolved why HaShem chose to teach this principle of derivation for the entire Torah specifically in this parashah and not in another parashah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:50.444772699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}